Hi,

sorry, it turns out that you also have to use the unsupported CDF for
the GCRMA step.  It is only needed for that step, hence the setCdf():s
set & undo.  You can download a binary version of HuEx-1_0-st-v2.cdf
at:

  http://aroma-project.org/chipTypes/HuEx-1_0-st-v2

Then do:

library("aroma.affymetrix");
verbose <- Arguments$getVerbose(-10, timestamp=TRUE);

dataSet <- "Exon Data";
chipType <- "HuEx-1_0-st-v2";

# The unsupported CDF
cdfS <- AffymetrixCdfFile$byChipType(chipType);
print(cdfS);

# The custom CDF

cdf <- AffymetrixCdfFile$byChipType(chipType,tags="fullR3,A20071112,EP");
print(cdf);

# Setup data set
csR <- AffymetrixCelSet$byName(dataSet, cdf=cdf);

# GCRMA background correction
setCdf(csR, cdfS); # Set temporarily

bc <- GcRmaBackgroundCorrection(csR, type="affinities");
print(bc);
csB <- process(bc, verbose=verbose);

setCdf(csR, cdf); # Undo.
setCdf(csB, cdf); # Undo.
print(csB);

That should do it.

FYI, when doing AffymetrixCelSet$byName(...) specify either argument
'chipType' or 'cdf' - not both.

/Henrik

